# Application-specific configuration.
#
# This file is the Kconfig root for the application, so it must pull in
# Zephyr's own tree first; otherwise every Zephyr symbol is undefined.
#
# These are the values that a reviewer or a test build is expected to change
# without touching source. The 750 ms window, the 10 s deployment indication,
# the 5 s alarm and the 500 ms blink period are *not* configurable: they are
# the behaviour the assignment specifies.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"

menu "Rocket demo"

config APP_APOGEE_MIN_ALT_CM
	int "Minimum altitude above the baseline before deploying (cm)"
	range 10 3000
	default 150
	help
	  Threshold relative to the baseline P0 captured at start-up, not to sea
	  level. 150 cm is about twice the altitude noise measured on the bench
	  (0.9 m peak-to-peak). A bench value, not a flight value: a real vehicle
	  would set this well above the ground handling envelope.

config APP_APOGEE_MIN_DESCENT_MM_S
	int "Minimum average descent over 750 ms (mm/s)"
	range 0 20000
	default 300
	help
	  How far below zero the 750 ms average velocity must be. 0 is the literal
	  "becomes negative" of the assignment; 300 mm/s is a noise guard above it,
	  not a performance threshold.

	  Timing: falling from rest at apogee, a 0.3 m/s trailing average is
	  reached about 0.41 s later, roughly 0.8 m below the peak. Raising this
	  value delays detection; it does not improve it in flight.

	  Note that a moving vehicle is not a bench: in the lab, room air drift
	  alone wanders by up to 0.55 m/s, which is why bench.conf needs a *larger*
	  margin than this default.

config APP_READY_INDICATION
	bool "Flash the LED twice when the system is ready"
	default y
	help
	  Once the sensor is answering, the baseline is frozen and the 750 ms
	  history is full, flash the LED twice (100 ms on, 120 ms off, 100 ms on).
	  This exists for untethered runs where no console is available.
	  It is not part of the assignment's LED behaviour; disable it to keep the
	  LED strictly for deployment and overheating.

endmenu
